// CRITICAL: The insert MUST go BETWEEN appendRewindMarker and leaveNote, not after leaveNote.
// leaveNote injects a mulligan:note CustomMessage into the LLM context (spec/02 C8). Calling it for a
// failed persist leaves a STRAY note referencing a rewind that never happened. The guard prevents that.

// CRITICAL: refusal(reason, granularity) already returns `details: { granularity }` (NO markerId).
// The contract's "details.markerId stays absent" is satisfied by REUSING refusal() — do NOT hand-build
// a result with markerId:null. The RewindDetails interface has markerId?: string | null (optional),
// so omitting it is type-correct.

// CRITICAL: The existing test `mulligan_rewind — leafId null fallback` (~line 646) BREAKS after the
// insert (it asserts /^Mulligan: rewound/ for getLeafId:null). It encodes the OLD buggy contract.
// It MUST be updated to assert the NEW refusal contract, or `npm test` will fail post-implementation.

// CRITICAL: In makePi, `appendEntry` throws BEFORE the push (`if (opts.throwOnAppend) throw; appended.push`).
// So `appended.length === 0` when throwOnAppend is true. The contract says "appendEntry attempted exactly
// once" — ATTEMPTED = the CALL was made once, regardless of whether it pushed. The `appended` array proves
// the call for case B (getLeafId null: push succeeds, THEN null leaf) but NOT for case A (throw).
// Add `appendEntryCalls: number` to makePi, incremented at the TOP of appendEntry (before the throw),
// and assert `appendEntryCalls === 1` in BOTH cases. This is the cleanest hand-rolled equivalent of a
// vi.fn() call-count assertion and matches the existing no-vi.fn() idiom.

// CRITICAL: Do NOT remove `?? toolCallId` from the leaveNote call. The contract says keep the success
// path unchanged. After the guard, markerId is guaranteed non-null on the success path, so `?? toolCallId`
// is dead-but-harmless. Removing it is out of scope and risks touching the success-path contract.

