## Implementation Blueprint

### The exact code edit (verified file:line)

**Edit 1 — `src/tools/rewind.ts` lines 463–465** (inside `rewindExecute`, step 7):
```typescript
// OLD (current):
    const markerId = appendRewindMarker(pi, ctx, payload);
    leaveNote(pi, { content: rendered, rewindId: markerId ?? toolCallId });

// NEW:
    const markerId = appendRewindMarker(pi, ctx, payload);
    if (markerId === null) {
      return refusal(
        "failed to persist the rewind marker (nothing will be hidden); no changes were made",
        granularity,
      );
    }
    leaveNote(pi, { content: rendered, rewindId: markerId ?? toolCallId });
```
Everything else in step 7 (the mutation-warning `hasWarning` computation, `successText(...)`, the `details: { granularity, k, ledger, markerId }` return) stays UNCHANGED. The `markerId` in that final `details` is now guaranteed non-null because the guard returns early on null.

Also update the step-7 inline comment (~line 461 `// (7) persist (step 7). excludeToolCallId === toolCallId...`) to note the null-check (e.g. append: `// If the marker could not be persisted (null — appendEntry threw or getLeafId returned null), refuse BEFORE leaveNote so no stray note is sent for a failed rewind (BUG-005).`) so the comment does not contradict the new guard.

### Test updates

**Task A — Extend `makePi` with an `appendEntryCalls` counter** (test/tools/rewind.test.ts ~line 58):
```typescript
// In makePi, add a call counter incremented BEFORE the throw check:
function makePi(opts: { throwOnAppend?: boolean; throwOnSendMessage?: boolean } = {}) {
  const appended: { customType: string; data: unknown }[] = [];
  const sent: { ... }[] = [];
  let appendEntryCalls = 0;                                  // NEW
  const pi = {
    appendEntry(customType: string, data?: unknown) {
      appendEntryCalls += 1;                                 // NEW — before the throw
      if (opts.throwOnAppend) throw new Error("appendEntry boom");
      appended.push({ customType, data });
    },
    sendMessage(...) { ... },
  };
  return { appended, sent, appendEntryCalls: () => appendEntryCalls, pi: pi as unknown as ExtensionAPI };
  // expose as a getter (closure) so the test reads the live count after run()
}
```
(Expose `appendEntryCalls` as a closure getter — `appendEntryCalls: () => appendEntryCalls` — so the test reads the count AFTER `run()` completes. Do NOT return the bare number (it would snapshot at construction.)

**Task B — UPDATE the breaking test** (test/tools/rewind.test.ts ~line 646, `describe("mulligan_rewind — leafId null fallback")`):
Replace the old assertion `/^Mulligan: rewound/` with the new refusal contract. Either repurpose the existing `it` or replace the whole describe. New shape:
