## Anti-Patterns to Avoid
- ❌ Do NOT hand-build a result with `markerId: null` for the refusal — reuse `refusal(reason, granularity)`, which omits markerId by construction.
- ❌ Do NOT move the guard AFTER `leaveNote` — that defeats the purpose (a stray note would still be sent).
- ❌ Do NOT change `appendRewindMarker` (src/markers.ts) to throw — it is fail-open by design (spec/03 principle #4, spec/08 E13); the guard belongs in the TOOL.
- ❌ Do NOT remove `?? toolCallId` from the leaveNote call — the contract says keep the success path unchanged (it is dead-but-harmless post-guard).
- ❌ Do NOT touch `countRewindMarkers`, `checkpointExists`, `resolvePreview`, or any filter/transform logic — those are BUG-004 / other work.
- ❌ Do NOT leave the old `leafId null fallback` test in place — its `/^Mulligan: rewound/` assertion encodes the bug and will fail post-insert.
- ❌ Do NOT assert `appended.toHaveLength(1)` in the appendEntry-throws case — the fake throws BEFORE the push, so `appended` is empty there; use the `appendEntryCalls` counter to prove the attempt.
- ❌ Do NOT delete or move any pipeline-state file (PRD.md, PRP.md, tasks.json, plan/*).
- ❌ Do NOT use vi.fn() — the house idiom is hand-rolled fakes; model the `appendEntryCalls` counter on the existing `appended`/`sent` array pattern.

## Confidence Score: 9/10
The change is 3 lines of source (one null-check reusing an existing helper) + a precisely-identified test update + one new 2-case describe block. No type changes, no new files, no API change, no filter/transform logic. The only subtlety is the `appended`-array-vs-`appendEntryCalls`-counter distinction in the throw case (the fake throws before push), which is fully resolved above by adding a closure counter to makePi. The single implementation risk is forgetting to update/remove the old `leafId null fallback` test — called out explicitly so it will not be missed.
